From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:20:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] test(test-backend-ops): add perf cases for the top-k argsort
 hint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The perf mode reads its own case list, so without these cases
`test-backend-ops perf -o ARGSORT_TOP_K` runs nothing. The 512-wide rows
match the MoE router at tg (1 and 4 rows) and pp512 (512 rows) and take
the partial sort. The [39,22] and [64,3] rows take the full sort and act
as a control.

🤖 Generated with Claude Code

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PSPFwkoM7cKXVVQWfzQpjs
---
 tests/test-backend-ops.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp b/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
index c07c29ff2..be861c542 100644
--- a/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
+++ b/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
@@ -12351,6 +12351,13 @@ static std::vector<std::unique_ptr<test_case>> make_test_cases_perf() {
     test_cases.emplace_back(new test_argsort(GGML_TYPE_F32, {200000, 1,  1, 1}));
     test_cases.emplace_back(new test_argsort(GGML_TYPE_F32, {200000, 16, 1, 1}));
 
+    // MoE routing: the tg and pp512 rows take the partial sort, the last two take the full sort
+    for (int64_t nrows : {1, 4, 512}) {
+        test_cases.emplace_back(new test_argsort_top_k(GGML_TYPE_F32, {512, nrows, 1, 1}, 10));
+    }
+    test_cases.emplace_back(new test_argsort_top_k(GGML_TYPE_F32, {39, 22, 1, 1}, 10));
+    test_cases.emplace_back(new test_argsort_top_k(GGML_TYPE_F32, {64, 3, 1, 1}, 64));
+
     test_cases.emplace_back(new test_top_k(GGML_TYPE_F32, {2, 1, 1, 1}, 1));
     // widths around the tiling threshold
     for (auto cols : {4096, 8192, 12288, 16384, 24576, 32768, 65536, 131072}) {
